## Objective
- Implement phase-095 in `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`: expose the already-linked `regex` crate to Redblue programs through a new `regex` module, with tests/docs and all four gates green.
- Required surface: `regex.match`, `regex.is_match`, `regex.capture`, `regex.replace`, `regex.split`; match records must compare by captured data, not identity; both tree-walker and bytecode VM must agree.

## Important Details
- Work only inside `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`; scratch space is `./target/tmp/`. Never write `/tmp`, `/home`, `rbops/`, `.github/workflows/`, `.opencode/agent/`, or `rbops/phases.json`.
- `regex` is already a dependency: `Cargo.toml:31` (and dev-dep at `Cargo.toml:41`), locked at `regex 1.13.1`.
- `end` is a reserved word, so match-record fields are `text`, `start`, `finish`, `groups` — **not** `end`.
- `test` is a reserved word, so the boolean function is `regex.is_match`, not `regex.test`.
- Match record semantics: `groups[0]` = whole match, `groups[n]` = capture group n; nonparticipating group = `nothing`; `start`/`finish` are character offsets, not bytes.
- Error contract: invalid pattern → `Error::Runtime` containing `regex pattern ... is not valid: ...`; invalid `$N`/`$name` replacement → `Error::Runtime` naming the missing group; `regex.capture` out-of-bounds → `Error::Runtime`; no Rust panics.
- `text.split` remains literal; only its comment in `src/stdlib.rs` was corrected. `regex.split` is the pattern form.
- Catastrophic pattern `(a+)+$` on 10,000 `a`s + `!` is tested and returns `yes`/`no` false quickly; `regex` crate is linear-time.
- The old SURVEY gap test `regex_is_refused_by_a_program_and_the_crate_is_reachable_only_from_tests` was replaced with `regex_is_answerable_by_a_program_on_both_engines`; `SURVEY.md` now marks rank 2 closed by phase-095 and counts 74 builtins / 12 modules / 52 members.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` passes.
- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.
- Full-suite output is saved at `target/tmp/full-test.log`; use it to find remaining failures.
- Correct verify invocation from the working directory is `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-095"` (there is no local `./rbops/verify.sh`).
